From 9bb2ed497a7671c17b147e156628c7ae54b019e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kestrel <kestrel@invalid>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 06:49:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] Add NameWindowsMemory: name Windows private memory's
 mappings by owner (default off)

Every NameWindowsMemory seconds a FEX-internal thread walks committed Windows
private memory and names its Linux mappings (PR_SET_VMA_ANON_NAME): win:heap
(Wine heaps: each heap, its subheaps and large blocks), win:stack (guard page),
win:exec (executable), win:gc (reservation of 16 GB or more), win:big (256 MB or
more), win:private. Ranges FEX named for itself are recorded and never
relabelled (kept in a fixed array: recording must not allocate, since FEX's
allocator names its own maps through the same call); a refused name no longer turns FEX's own naming off. The worker starts
with the process's second thread, never during process init, and its first pass
waits at least 30 s. Heaps are found with ntdll's RtlGetProcessHeaps and
RtlLockHeap: the emulator DLL must import nothing but ntdll, since it loads
before kernelbase.
